--
^warning: ignoring
dropping inline assembly
--
Inline-assembly statements containing an unrecognized instruction are
approximated conservatively by the remove_asm pass: output operands, the
objects pointer operands point to, with a "memory" clobber the objects of
static lifetime, what these point to, and address-taken local variables, and
the rounding mode are assigned nondeterministic values.
See GitHub issue diffblue/cbmc#6374.
